    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Find the equation of the tangent to the curve $y=\\dfrac{4}{x}$ at $\\left(8,\\dfrac{1}{2}\\right)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x+16y-16=0$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{dy}{dx}&=-\\frac{4}{x^2}\\\\\nm&=-\\frac{4}{8^2}\\\\\nm&=-\\frac{1}{16}\n\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $y-y_1=m(x-x_1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\ny-\\frac12&=-\\frac1{16}(x-8)\\\\\n16y-8&=-x+8\\\\\nx+16y-16&=0\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
